WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
Every Aztec transaction

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.160
pays a network fee,

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.520
the way Ethereum charges gas.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.920
The fee is paid in Fee Juice,

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.880
the token that pays network fees on Aztec.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.640
You bring it over from Ethereum,

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.120
and it is used only for fees.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.320
The price depends on the work:

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.160
publishing the transaction's data,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.120
and running it on the network.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.160
Nulo shows you the fee before you send.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.080
How you pay matters.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.680
Pay with public Fee Juice,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.120
and the record names you as the payer,

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.120
each time.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.840
Pay with private Fee Juice,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.320
and the payer on record is a

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.640
contract many people share.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.960
Sometimes the fee is sponsored:

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.640
someone else pays it for you.
